    "updated_at": "2020-06-24T02:46:48Z",
    "body": "Thanks Lim! 😄 \r\n\r\nHere are a few things that may fix the problem. Please try them one at a time and see if a new terminal + fish instance behaves correctly.\r\n- In iTerm, go to Preferences > Profiles > Text, and enable \"Use Unicode version 9+ widths\"\r\n- In iTerm, go to Preferences > Profiles > Text, and enable \"Ambiguous characters are double-width\"\r\n- Add this one-liner to your `~/.config/fish/config.fish`:\r\n  ```fish\r\n  set -g fish_emoji_width 2\r\n  ```",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
